      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اغتار</span></b>  <i>He procured</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِيرَة</span> [<i>a provision of corn,</i>
or <i>wheat,</i> &amp;c.]. (K.) You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَرَجَ يَغْتَارُ لِأَهْلِهِ</span>
<i>He went forth to procure</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ميرة</span> <i>for his family.</i>
(Fr, Sgh.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He derived,</i> or <i>obtained, benefit,
advantage,</i> or <i>profit.</i> (TA.) See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غور</span>.

